---
import { customers } from './facts.mjs';
---
<figure class="access-figure" data-boundary aria-labelledby="boundary-caption">
 <figcaption id="boundary-caption"><span class="figure-number">Figure 2</span> A table grant and a tenant boundary</figcaption>
 <div class="access-scene">
  <div class="identity-strip"><span>Request authorised for <b>tenant 10</b></span><span>Database login <code>shop_runtime</code></span><span>Policy context <b>10</b></span></div>
  <pre class="query-line">SELECT customer_id, name
FROM customers
ORDER BY customer_id;</pre>
  <p class="stage-label" data-stage data-live>1. Check the table privilege</p>
  <div class="customer-grid">
   {customers.map(row=><div class="customer-row" data-customer={row.id}><span>Tenant {row.tenant}</span><b>{row.id} · {row.name}</b><span class="row-verdict" data-live>Awaiting query</span></div>)}
  </div>
  <div class="result-line" data-result data-live>Result: query has not run.</div>
  <p class="access-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The connection is shop_runtime. Its SELECT grant permits reading these customer columns. That grant alone does not choose a tenant.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="access-controls">
  <label>Row boundary <select data-boundary-choice><option value="policy">Tenant policy</option><option value="none">Table grant only</option></select></label>
  <div class="playback" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div>
  <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="access-caption">A model of an omitted tenant condition. The source table is the same in both settings. With a tenant policy and context 10, Rowan’s row stays stored but does not enter this result.</p>
 <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>The source contains Mina Shah, Tariq Aziz and Edda Berg in tenant 10, and Rowan Vale in tenant 20. Table access alone returns all four. The illustrated policy compares each row’s tenant ID with context 10 and returns only the first three. Neither setting checks the signed-in person’s right to select that context.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import { customers, boundarySteps } from './facts.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-boundary]').forEach(root=>{
  const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-boundary-choice]')!;
  const stages=['1. Check the table privilege','2. Run the query','3. Apply the row boundary','4. Return the visible rows'];
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:step=>{
   const policy=choice.value==='policy';
   root.querySelector('[data-stage]')!.textContent=stages[step];
   root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=boundarySteps[step];
   customers.forEach(row=>{const el=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-customer="${row.id}"]`)!; const excluded=policy&&row.tenant!==10;
    el.dataset.verdict=step<2?'waiting':excluded?'excluded':'included';
    el.querySelector('.row-verdict')!.textContent=step<2?'Awaiting query':excluded?'Excluded: tenant differs':'Included in result';
   });
   root.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=step<3?'Result: query has not returned.':policy?'Result: 1 Mina, 2 Tariq, 3 Edda. Rowan is hidden.':'Result: 1 Mina, 2 Tariq, 3 Edda, 4 Rowan. Tenant 20 is exposed.';
  }}); choice.addEventListener('change',player.render);
 });
</script>
